 "case": "N28-CANDIDATE-NEG",
 "says": "A person captures the memory of one selected transcript span (source.observe, then source.capture.record) and stores a candidate choice extracted from that capture (memory.candidate.store), which the owner writes as version 1 naming the capture and the exact span bytes as its origin. The person then edits the proposal, changing the chosen synchronous mode, and submits it under the same candidate id; the owner writes version 2, and its origin is the origin of version 1, byte for byte. The person then rejects the candidate (memory.candidate.reject); the owner writes version 3 standing rejected, and its origin is still that of version 2. Every memory_candidate the owner returns keeps the origin of the version it replaces: none restates the captured candidate as written by hand and none names another capture, which are the breaking records of the rule fixture candidate_keeps_its_origin. Neither the edit nor the rejection changes the capture, the observed span or any destination source.",
